  {
    "name": "Fitness Classes: Tabata",
    "type": "Recreation Calendar",
    "public": false,
    "description": "Class Description: Tabata is a style of cardio conditioning with 20 seconds of maximum effort, followed by 10 seconds of rest for 4 minutes. We will start with a warm-up, do several intervals and end with a cool down. Good for endurance! \n\nFitness Classes are open to all students, staff and faculty! There is no need to sign up for the class, just arrive 5 minutes before the start of class and bring some water! You are welcome to bring your own equipment, yoga mat or tennis racket but if you do not have your own equipment, you are welcome to check the equipment out from the Rec Office, Gym 151.",
